\id 1PE - Open English Translation—Readers’ Version (OET-RV) v0.2.5
\usfm 3.0
\ide UTF-8
\h 1 Peter
\toc1 The first letter from Simon ‘the Rock’
\toc2 1 Peter
\mt2 The first letter from
\mt1 Simon ‘the Rock’
\mt2 (Peter or Peter)
\rem This is still an early look into the unpolished text of the Open English Translation of the Bible. Please double-check the text in advance before using in public.
\c 1
\p
\v 1 \add This letter is from\add* Peter, an ambassador for Jesus \add the\add* messiah.
\p \add It’s written\add* to those people who’ve been chosen \add by God\add* and dispersed \add by persecution\add* throughout \add the provinces of\add* Pontus, Galatia, Cappadocia, Asia \add Minor\add*, and Bithynia.
\v 2 \add They were chosen\add* in advance by God the father by his pure spirit, thanks to the obedience of Jesus \add the\add* messiah and the sprinkling of his blood.
\p May \add God give\add* you grace and abundant peace.
\s1 The future hope of life without ending
\p
\v 3 May God, the father of our master Jesus \add the\add* messiah be blessed. He’s the one who, because of his incredible mercy, births us into living hope through the death and coming back to life of Jesus \add the\add* messiah.
\v 4 \add Now we have\add* an inheritance that can’t be destroyed or ruined and never diminishes. It’s kept in the heavens for you \add chosen people\add*,
\v 5 who are guarded through faith by God’s power, because the rescue is ready to be revealed in the final age.
\p
\v 6 \add This rescue\add* brings some happiness now, although offset by the sorrow of various trials \add that you go through\add*
\v 7 in order that your faith will be purified by fire, like gold, but \add even\add* more precious, because gold corrodes. Then your faith will lead to praise and glory and honour when Jesus \add the\add* messiah is revealed,
\v 8 the one you \add chosen people\add* love, even though you’ve never seen him. Yet you believe, and because of that, you’re happier than you can even show, AND HAVING BEEN GLORIFIED,
\v 9 you’ll receive the result of your faith, which is that your souls are rescued.
\p
\v 10 The prophets wanted that rescue and searched for it, even while speaking about the grace which you \add chosen people\add* would experience.
\v 11 They tried to discover which person or what time the messiah’s spirit within them was telling them about, having previously testified that \add the\add* messiah would suffer but afterwards would be GLORIOUS.
\v 12 It was shown to them that they weren’t just serving themselves, but were serving you as they declared all the same things that have been preached to you by \add the\add* holy spirit who was sent from heaven. Even God’s messengers in heaven wanted to know more about those things.
\s1 The holy behaviour of believers
\p
\v 13 So take this seriously and get your minds prepared, putting your full hope in the grace that’ll be brought to you by Jesus \add the\add* messiah being revealed.
\v 14 As people who want to obey, don’t conform to your earlier desires that came from your ignorance,
\v 15 but just as God who called you is holy, your yourselves need to be holy in all your conduct,
\v 16 because it’s been written that ‘you’ll be holy \add people\add* because I am holy.’
\p
\v 17 And since you call on the father who impartially judges each person according to their actions, continue to obey him even as you live as foreigners,
\v 18 knowing that when you were in slavery due to your poor conduct that you inherited from your ancestors, you weren’t bought out of that by payment of things that decay like silver or gold,
\v 19 but by the precious blood of \add the\add* messiah—the unblemished and spotless lamb.
\v 20 He’d been known before the world was created, yet he was only recently revealed for the sake of you \add chosen people\add*
\v 21 who believe in God through him. God was the one who raised him from the dead and honoured him, so that your faith and hope would be in God.
\p
\v 22 Since your souls have been purified by obeying the truth, \add now\add* you should love each other from your hearts and without hypocrisy.
\v 23 You’ve been born again, not \add growing\add* from some physical thing that’ll decay, but from indestructible material—God’s message that’s alive and lives on,
\v 24 because \add it’s written\add*:
\q1 ‘All flesh is like grass,
\q2 and the beauty of our bodies like its flower.
\q1 The grass will wither and its flower will drop,
\q2
\v 25 but Yahweh’s message will last till the end of the age.’
\m And that’s the good message that’s been preached to you \add chosen people\add*.
\c 2
\p
\v 1 So then, get rid of all malice and deceit, and hypocrisy and envy, and slandering \add others\add*.
\v 2 \add Just\add* like newborn babies long for pure milk so they’ll grow, you should cultivate a thirst for what’ll help you grow as people who are rescued,
\v 3 since you’ve tasted that Yahweh is good.
\s1 The vital building-stone and the believers
\p
\v 4 As you \add chosen people\add* approach the living building-stone (which was rejected by humans yet chosen and honoured by God),
\v 5 you’re being built into a temple and \add joining\add* a holy group of priests to offer up \em spiritual\em* sacrifices that are acceptable to God through Jesus \add the\add* messiah,
\v 6 because it’s written in the scriptures:
\q1 ‘Look, I’m placing a building-stone in Zion,
\q2 the \add vital\add* cornerstone that’s chosen and honoured,
\q2 and anyone who believes in him certainly won’t be disgraced.’
\m
\v 7 To all of you who believe, this \add cornerstone\add* is valuable, but to those who don’t believe:
\q1 ‘The building-stone which the builders rejected
\q2 ended up becoming the \add vital\add* cornerstone.’
\m
\v 8 and \add he’ll be\add*:
\q1 ‘A stone that people stumble over
\q2 and a rock that upsets people.’
\m They stumble \add because\add* they won’t believe in the message—that is what was appointed for them.
\p
\v 9 But you \add believers\add* are a chosen tribe, a group of royal priests, a holy nation, a people group that God has procured, so that you can tell others about the virtues of the one who called you out of darkness and into his marvellous light.
\v 10 Previously you weren’t a people group, but now you’re God’s people—previously you hadn’t been shown mercy, but now you have been.
\s1 Battling worldly desires
\p
\v 11 Dear friends, I’m urging you as travellers and foreigners to keep away from the world’s temptations, which are in a battle against your soul.
\v 12 Even as you, \add friends\add*, live among the world’s people, maintain your good conduct so that when they slander you by calling you ‘evil’, at the time of God’s \add judgement\add* they’ll have to honour god when they see your good behaviour.
\p
\v 13 Submit yourselves to every human authority, because \add you obey\add* the master, whether it’s to the king who rules,
\v 14 or the governors he sends to punish those who do evil and to praise those who do good.
\v 15 God wants you \add chosen people\add* to silence the ignorant \add talk\add* of foolish people by doing good.
\v 16 Live like free \add people\add*, but don’t use that freedom to cover up evil—use it as God’s slaves.
\v 17 Honour others and be loving towards your fellow believers. Revere God as well as honouring the king.
\s1 Doing good despite suffering
\p
\v 18 You who are house-servants should respectfully obey your masters—not only the good and gentle \add ones\add*, but also the crooked \add ones\add*,
\v 19 because \add God\add* favours those who endure unjust hardships because of their godly consciences.
\v 20 What good would it do if you were enduring being beaten because of doing evil? But if you endure suffering for doing good, then God will be pleased \add with your behaviour\add*,
\v 21 because that’s what we’re called to, because \add the\add* messiah also suffered for you \add chosen people\add*. He left an example for you, so that you can follow in his steps:
\v 22 he didn’t do evil or say anything that wasn’t true,
\v 23 when he was insulted he didn’t retaliate, when he was persecuted he didn’t threaten, but put his trust in the one who’ll judge \add everyone\add* with \add true\add* justice.
\v 24 He sacrificed his own body on the \add wooden\add* post for \em our\em* sins, so that when we die to sin we can live for righteousness. By his wounds, you \add chosen people\add* were healed.
\v 25 \add He did all that\add* because you were like lost sheep, but now you’ve returned to your souls’ shepherd and overseer.
\c 3
\s1 Advice to married couples
\p
\v 1 Similarly, women should be subject to their husbands, so that if any of them don’t believe the message, they’ll be won by their wives’ behaviour even without \add hearing\add* the message,
\v 2 because they’ll be able to observe \add their wives’\add* pure behaviour.
\v 3 \add These women shouldn’t focus\add* on outward \add appearances\add* like elaborate hairstyles, or gold \add jewellery\add* or \add expensive\add* clothes,
\v 4 but on the inner person with a gentle and quiet spirit that’s indestructible and which God \add considers\add* precious.
\v 5 That was how holy women \add in the past\add* adorned themselves—those whose hope was in God,
\v 6 like Sarah, who submitted to Abraham who you’ve become descendants of. She called him ‘master’, doing good and without any worries.
\p
\v 7 Similarly, men should live with \add their wives\add* with understanding, like how you’d handle something more fragile. They should display honour to their fellow recipients of life-\add giving\add* grace so that their prayers won’t be hindered.
\s1 Suffering for doing good
\p
\v 8 Finally, everyone should be agreeable and sympathetic \add to others\add*, kind and caring towards those around you, humble
\v 9 and not repaying evil with evil or insult with insult, but rather be a blessing to others. You were called to do that so that you \add chosen people\add* can receive a blessing,
\v 10 because \add it’s written\add*:
\q1 ‘The person wanting to enjoy life and see good days,
\q1 let their tongue cease from evil,
\q2 and their lips not speak deceit.
\q1
\v 11 Let them turn away from evil and do good,
\q1 let them look for peace and chase after it,
\q1
\v 12 because Yahweh looks kindly on the righteous,
\q2 and his ears listen to their petition,
\q1 ^but Yahweh \add turns\add* his face away from those who do evil.’
\p
\v 13 Who’s going to mistreat you if you \add chosen people\add* start actively \add doing\add* good?
\v 14 But even if some of you do suffer because of your godliness, \add you will be\add* blessed. Don’t be scared or disturbed because of your fear of them,
\v 15 but revere the messiah as the master of your hearts. Always be ready to explain the hope that you \add chosen people\add* have if anyone asks,
\v 16 but \add do it\add* with gentleness and respect, keeping a clear conscience, so that if you’re falsely accused of doing evil, then the ones who’ll be disgraced will be the ones who mistreat you \add chosen people, because of\add* the good way you live because of the message.
\v 17 After all, it’s better to do good, and then, if God intends it, to suffer, than to do evil,
\v 18 because \add the\add* messiah also died once for sin, that is, the sinless one died for sinful people, so that he can bring you \add chosen people past death\add* onward to God. \add Although\add* he experienced physical death, he’d been given life in \add the\add* spirit,
\v 19 and with that life he also went to the spirits in prison and preached to them—
\v 20 those who’d refused to believe. God had waited patiently in Noah’s time when the barge was being built, \add yet\add* only a few were saved. Eight of them were brought safely through the waters,
\v 21 which also represents how being immersed saved you \add chosen people\add*. It doesn’t remove the filth from your bodies, but cleans the conscience as you make a pledge to God based on the coming back to life of Jesus \add the\add* messiah,
\v 22 who went to heaven and \add sat\add* at God’s right, with God’s messengers and authorities and powers all under his authority.
\c 4
\s1 Leaving worldly desires behind
\p
\v 1 Since \add the\add* messiah suffered physically, you \add chosen people\add* should also cultivate the same intention, because anyone who suffers physically stops sinning
\v 2 so that they can live their remaining physical lives obeying God’s intentions instead of this world’s lusts,
\v 3 because enough time has been spent \add listening to\add* this world’s advice and pursuing immorality, lusts, drunkenness, carousing, drinking parties, and repulsive service to false gods.
\v 4 \add The unbelievers\add* will be surprised that you \add chosen people\add* aren’t joining them in that unrestrained, wild living, and they’ll mock you,
\v 5 but they’ll \add need\add* to give an account \add for their actions\add* to the one who’s ready to judge \add both\add* the living and the dead.
\v 6 That’s why the good message was preached even to the dead, so that while people might judge them according to this world’s standards, yet they might live spiritually according to God’s judgement.
\p
\v 7 The end of everything is getting close, so make good decisions and be serious in prayer,
\v 8 and more than anything, display genuine love to each other, because love triumphs over many sins.
\v 9 Show hospitality to each other without grumbling.
\v 10 Whatever gift each person has received, they should use it to serve the others as good managers of the various \add forms of\add* grace God’s \add given us\add*.
\v 11 Anyone who shares wisdom that came from God or uses the strength that God’s given them to serve \add others\add* needs to be honouring God through Jesus \add the\add* messiah. He’s the one who \add deserves\add* the honour and power throughout all time.
\s1 The suffering of believers
\p
\v 12 Dear friends, don’t be surprised about the fiery trials that you’ll have to face as a test, as though it’s something unusual that’s happening to you,
\v 13 but rather, as you, \add friends\add*, share in the messiah’s sufferings, stay positive so that you’ll be happy, just as you’re glad to see his honour revealed.
\v 14 You, \add friends\add*, \add will be\add* blessed if you’re derided in the messiah’s name, because God’s spirit rests on you—the spirit that honours \add him\add*.
\v 15 None of you should suffer \add persecution\add* because you’re a murderer or a thief or a troublemaker or nosey-parker,
\v 16 but if you \add suffer\add* for being one of the messiah’s people, then there’s no need to feel ashamed, but \add instead\add* praise God in that name.
\p
\v 17 It’s time for the judgement to begin—and to begin with God’s people—and if we’re judged first, what will the outcome be for those who refuse to believe in God’s good message?
\v 18 Yes,
\q1 ‘if it’s difficult for godly people to be saved,
\q2 ^what will it be like for the ungodly and for sinners?’
\m
\v 19 So for everyone who’s suffering according to God’s intentions, let them entrust their souls’ well-being to the faithful creator.
\c 5
\s1 Advice to believers
\p
\v 1 Because of that, I’m encouraging your elders, as a fellow elder, and a witness of the messiah’s sufferings, and also a partner in the GLORY that’s going to be revealed:
\v 2 Carefully shepherd God’s people that you care for, not out of compulsion, but willingly, listening to God, not greedily, but enthusiastically,
\v 3 not exercising dominance over them, but being examples for them.
\v 4 Then when the chief shepherd \add returns\add*, you \add elders\add* will receive the unfading crown of honour.
\p
\v 5 Similarly, you younger ones, take your elders’ advice, and all of you, show humility to each other, because ‘God opposes those who are proud, but displays grace to those who are humble.’
\v 6 So humble yourselves under God’s mighty hand so that he might honour you at the \add right\add* time.
\v 7 Give all your concerns to him because he cares about you all.
\p
\v 8 Stay alert and keep watch. Your opponent, the devil, walks around like a roaring lion, wanting to swallow up \add you chosen people\add*,
\v 9 \add but you should remain\add* firmly in the faith and resist him, knowing that fellow believers \add all around\add* the world experiencing similar suffering are doing the same.
\v 10 Then God, \add the source\add* of all grace, and the one who called you to his eternal GLORY in \add the\add* messiah, will prepare you \add chosen people\add* as you suffer a little, and will then strengthen you as you’re established.
\v 11 May his authority be powerful throughout all time. May it be so.
\s1 Farewell
\p
\v 12 I’ve written this brief \add letter\add* with the \add help\add* of the faithful brother, Silvanus, to encourage you \add chosen people\add* and to testify that God’s grace that you accepted is true.
\p
\v 13 The chosen \add group\add* in Babylon and my ‘son’ Mark send their greetings to you \add chosen people\add*.
\v 14 Greet one another with a kiss of love.
\p May all of you who are \add united with\add* \add the\add* messiah experience God’s peace.
